#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""readepub - a dependency-free terminal EPUB reader (Python 3.8+, stdlib only).

MathML equations are rendered as Unicode text (stacked fractions, matrices, roots,
scripts); inline math is flattened to one line.

Images are shown inline, in place, when the terminal supports a graphics
protocol (kitty/Ghostty/WezTerm via the kitty protocol, iTerm2/WezTerm via the
iTerm2 protocol); otherwise an "[Image: alt]" placeholder is shown.

Keys: space/f/PgDn page down   b/PgUp page up   j/k/arrows scroll a line
      right/left (or n/p when no search is active) next/previous chapter
      g/G top/bottom   / search   n/N next/previous match (Esc clears)
      t table of contents (j/k, Enter)   q quit

Kitty-protocol terminals only accept PNG; JPEG/GIF images are converted with
`sips` (macOS) or ImageMagick if one is installed, else shown as placeholders.
"""
